# Pinned Opengrep rule pack

`rules.yaml` is the rule pack pi-lens hands to Opengrep on first run, offline,
and until a refreshed pack is cached (#4765). It is a third-party work, not
pi-lens code; pi-lens itself stays MIT.

## Source and licence

- Source: <https://github.com/opengrep/opengrep-rules>, commit
  `f1d2b562b414783763fd02a6ed2736eaed622efa` (a fork of
  `semgrep/semgrep-rules` taken on 2024-12-13, before Semgrep moved its rules
  to the Semgrep Rules License).
- Licence of that commit, from its `LICENSE` file (copied verbatim beside this
  notice): "Commons Clause" License Condition v1.0 on `semgrep-rules`,
  "License: LGPL 2.1", "Licensor: Semgrep, Inc.". The full LGPL-2.1 text is
  `LGPL-2.1.txt`.
- Rule files carry `metadata.license: Commons Clause License Condition
  v1.0[LGPL-2.1-only]` or no licence field. One upstream rule is marked
  `proprietary license - copyright (c) Semgrep, Inc.`; it is excluded (see
